WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.630
2001.

2
00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:04.930
The census asks everyone
in England and Wales a new,

3
00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.180
voluntary question: what is your religion?

4
00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:12.240
That year, 71.7 per
cent answered Christian.

5
00:00:12.290 --> 00:00:17.260
By 2021, it was 46.2 per
cent: for the first time,

6
00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:18.880
fewer than half.

7
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:22.410
No religion had grown to 37.2 per cent.

8
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.300
Yet Christmas Day, Good Friday and
Easter Monday are still bank holidays.

9
00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.900
So why, if fewer than
half now tick Christian?

10
00:00:30.950 --> 00:00:35.390
In this mission, you'll read
the census from 2001 to 2021,

11
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:38.460
and find out what it
can and cannot tell us.

12
00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:42.900
Then you'll meet Britain's many
faiths, and atheists and humanists.

13
00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:47.370
Your mission: find out why Christmas
and Easter are still holidays when fewer

14
00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:49.080
than half tick Christian.
